<title>JAPAN: NSW launches 5.45% yen/A$ samurai due 1999--Nomura.</title>
<headline>NSW launches 5.45% yen/A$ samurai due 1999--Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar dual currency samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  New South Wales Treasury Corp</p>
<p> AMT		 35 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.45 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  13 April 1999</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  11 April 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 1 to April 9</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA, Moody's Aa2</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTES:  Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,114.04 for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
